    "description": "Set the first verifier to Sonnet 5.5 at medium effort by D4c E3\n\n## Summary\n\nE3 of D4c: the model and the effort of the first verifier. Version 0.18.0.\n\n- **The first verifier goes to Sonnet 5.5 at medium effort** (`ROLE_DEFAULTS.verifier.effort` changes from high to medium). On the 239 stored candidates of S1, it passes the rule for a cheaper arm. Its posted recall is 0.032 lower (90% interval -0.064 to 0.000), its posted precision is 0.011 higher, and it costs 0.62 times as much for each verification ($0.103 against $0.167).\n- **Opus 5.5 low fails both rules**: 1.09 times the cost, precision 0.023 lower, recall 0.032 lower. So Opus 5.5 medium did not run.\n- **Terra medium fails both rules** on its sample (the figures come from another session).\n- **The escalation:** the pipeline with its escalation has a posted recall of 0.536, against 0.496 for the first verifier alone, at 2.2 times the cost. The note gives this as a design question and does not change it.\n- The note `docs/research/e3-verifier-model.md` holds the method, the rules on made-up figures, every figure, the spend and the limits. The design doc and the model research note now name medium effort. E3 is marked done in TICKETS.md.\n\n## Spend\n\nThe paid runs cost $69.05: Sonnet 5.5 medium $24.84, Opus 5.5 low $43.66, and the judge $0.55. Every arm ran through `pr-review replay` on a frozen build of 03a87ee, with one shared judge cache. No call of any arm reached its cap.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` (1697 tests), `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`\n- [x] `scripts/check-version-bump.sh 03a87ee HEAD` gives 0.17.0 to 0.18.0\n- [x] Three tests that state the default effort of the verifier now state medium\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZg7V9Qr9viaw1dTW3s\n",
